Now we click on the fabric in the object window.

491
00:36:57,900 --> 00:37:02,900
In the attribute editor, you can see that there is a picture in the text.

492
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:08,900
We open the added project files, double click A, select the sixth garment.

493
00:37:08,900 --> 00:37:12,900
Press the left button of the JPG file, drag it to the text.

494
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:18,900
Change the picture.

495
00:37:18,900 --> 00:37:29,900
Then select the edit text tool in the second tool column.

496
00:37:29,900 --> 00:37:32,900
Right-click on any of the sliders.

497
00:37:32,900 --> 00:37:36,900
Here is a double arrow icon.

498
00:37:36,900 --> 00:37:39,900
This is the selection direction of the sliders.

499
00:37:39,900 --> 00:38:01,900
When we put the mouse in the middle of the four-way direction, the left and right mouse buttons and the moving mouse can move the position of the text.

500
00:38:01,900 --> 00:38:05,900
Put the mouse on both ends of the four-way direction.

501
00:38:05,900 --> 00:38:10,900
The left and right mouse buttons and the moving mouse can rotate the four-way direction.

502
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:13,900
When we press Shift, a curtain will appear.

503
00:38:13,900 --> 00:38:30,900
This curtain is 45 degrees or 90 degrees.

504
00:38:30,900 --> 00:38:43,900
Here, we only change the four-way direction of the board, without changing the direction of the texture of the fabric.

505
00:38:43,900 --> 00:38:55,900
At the upper right corner of the 2D window, there will be a texture editor made of three pullers and a circle.

506
00:38:55,900 --> 00:38:57,900
When we pull the puller,

507
00:38:57,900 --> 00:39:00,900
we can zoom in on the texture.

508
00:39:00,900 --> 00:39:08,900
We can also zoom out or zoom out.

509
00:39:09,900 --> 00:39:13,900
When we rotate the circle,

510
00:39:13,900 --> 00:39:22,900
we can feel the 45 or 90 degree curtain.

511
00:39:22,900 --> 00:39:25,900
Here, we only change the four-way direction of the texture of the material,

512
00:39:25,900 --> 00:39:29,900
without changing the direction of the texture of the board.

513
00:39:59,900 --> 00:40:06,900
Click on the triangle next to the texture and choose the fill color.

514
00:40:06,900 --> 00:40:11,900
Pull it down.

515
00:40:11,900 --> 00:40:17,900
Double click to open the color.

516
00:40:17,900 --> 00:40:27,900
You can use the straw tool to extract any color you see.

517
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:33,900
Total color to be extracted.

518
00:40:33,900 --> 00:40:49,900
You can also enter the RGB value.

519
00:40:49,900 --> 00:41:01,900
You can also choose the color in the Pantone color card on the right.

520
00:41:01,900 --> 00:41:08,900
Click OK.

521
00:41:08,900 --> 00:41:12,900
In the 3D window, select the tool to improve the quality of the clothing.

522
00:41:12,900 --> 00:41:15,900
Here you can reduce the particle thickness by one click.

523
00:41:15,900 --> 00:41:23,900
The thickness of the panel is the surface thickness of the virtual model.

524
00:41:23,900 --> 00:41:30,900
Click OK.

525
00:41:30,900 --> 00:41:36,900
Open the simulation and apply the settings to the 3D window.

526
00:41:36,900 --> 00:41:42,900
After the application is set, the computing power will increase and the simulation speed will be very slow.

527
00:41:42,900 --> 00:41:54,900
Therefore, it is not recommended to adjust the clothing at this stage.

528
00:41:54,900 --> 00:41:59,900
After the simulation is completed, turn off the simulation.

529
00:41:59,900 --> 00:42:03,900
In the main menu, select files.

530
00:42:03,900 --> 00:42:07,900
There are two options, stored as sample files and stored as.

531
00:42:07,900 --> 00:42:18,900
Stored as a sample file is to be covered and stored on the basis of the original file.

532
00:42:18,900 --> 00:42:22,900
Stored as has a sample and clothing.

533
00:42:22,900 --> 00:42:28,900
Stored as a sample is to store virtual models and 3D clothing at the same time in the same file corner.

534
00:42:29,900 --> 00:42:36,900
This is not a satisfy for such an option.

535
00:42:36,900 --> 00:42:39,900
Stored as a sample should be either stored in the 3D 3D model or not in the physical model.

536
00:42:39,900 --> 00:42:41,900
Stored as a sample should be stored in the window header section of the 3D 3D model3 sees is 3D 3D virtual model.

537
00:42:41,900 --> 00:42:47,900
So choose to sort as a sample.

538
00:42:47,900 --> 00:42:51,900
Enter a file name.

539
00:42:51,900 --> 00:42:53,900
hui

540
00:42:53,900 --> 00:42:56,900
No Chinese characters and special marks are possible.

541
00:42:56,900 --> 00:42:57,900
e

542
00:42:57,900 --> 00:43:02,900
Click save

543
00:43:02,900 --> 00:43:06,900
Here, this skirt is done

